🧠 Theory: Binary Search Kya Hota Hai?
🔹 1. Definition:
Binary Search ek algorithm hai jo sorted array mein kisi element ko dhoondhne ke liye use hota hai.

Ye har step mein array ko aadha-aadha karta hai, isliye iska naam "Binary" (do bhaag) Search hai.

🔹 2. Kaise Kaam Karta Hai?
Pura array lete hain (start = 0, end = n-1)

Beech wala element (mid) nikaalte hain.

Agar mid value hi target hai → 🎯 mil gaya.

Agar target chhoti hai → left half mein dhoondhte hain.

Agar target badi hai → right half mein dhoondhte hain.

Ye process tab tak repeat hoti hai jab tak element mil na jaaye ya search space khatam na ho jaaye.

🔹 3. Kaha Kaam Karta Hai?
Sirf sorted array ya list mein.

Time complexity: O(log n) → Bahut tezi se kaam karta hai.

📘 Algorithm (Steps)
low = 0, high = array.length - 1

Jab tak low <= high:

mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2)

Agar arr[mid] == target → return mid

Agar arr[mid] < target → low = mid + 1

Agar arr[mid] > target → high = mid - 1

Agar loop ke baad kuch nahi mila → return -1

✅ Aasaan Example Question:
Q: Array [1, 3, 5, 7, 9] mein number 5 ka index find karo using binary search.

🔹 Step-by-Step Dry Run:
low = 0, high = 4

mid = (0+4)/2 = 2, arr[2] = 5

🎯 arr[mid] == target, so answer is 2


